It depends on how much people are willing to pay for.

I have tested PMAZB-A on DEC3000/300 (150MHz 21064) expecting it would
show any difference from builtin single channel TCDS.  It might have
been faster or slower.  I composed 16 (or some) RZ28B drives
striped/concatenated with ccd psuedo devices in a single /300, and ran
disk performance measurements.  The result was simple; no gain nor
loss between them.  It's interesting to notice because /300 has
12.5MHz TC option slot while builtin TCDS is directly attached with
system bus.  Having PMAZC-A instead might bring a benefit or little
gain.

